cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  battery-design: an in-browser battery pack design, architecture and
  mission-simulation tool
message: >-
  If you use this tool, or figures produced by it, in a report, paper or tender
  document, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Varzandeh
    given-names: Morshed
repository-code: https://github.com/Morshedvarzandeh/battery-design
url: https://morshedvarzandeh.github.io/battery-design/
abstract: >-
  A browser-based battery pack designer that derives a complete concept design
  from an application and an available space: it packs every cell in its library
  into the given bay and ranks the results on energy, lifetime cost and mass;
  derives the electrical architecture (module partition, BMS topology and AFE
  count, precharge, contactors, fuse, isolation, DC-DC, communication bus);
  sizes the thermal system (loop, coolant flow, chiller duty, heater need);
  plans the sensor set by level; simulates the mission in time with an
  equivalent-circuit electrical model coupled to a lumped thermal model; and
  produces customer-facing reports. Every value is traced to a public datasheet
  or a named standard, and assumptions without a public source are listed
  explicitly. Output is first-order engineering guidance, not certification.
keywords:
  - battery pack design
  - lithium-ion
  - battery management system
  - thermal management
  - energy storage
  - electric vehicles
  - engineering design tool
  - simulation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-03'
